e filter through which this  should all be seen I'm here to tell you  I don't have such a lens for you because  I believe any such lens is too  simplistic now if you want that  simplistic analysis there are plenty  available there's no question about it  but to some degree we sometimes are  blinded by narrative and in some cases  if all you have is a hammer everything  looks like a nail meaning if you want to  see every issue as being related to one  problem you're able to find a way to do  that even if it's not really the right  or most robust analysis so I'm gonna  give you some examples and then we'll  get to what I think is a reasonable  analysis and way to think about all of  this so one story line we're hearing and  we've heard it from a lot of different  people is this is merely about race this  is about white cops killing black people  this is about white cops oppressing  black protesters this is about a  fundamentally racist justice system it's  about a fundamental fundamentally racist  society it's it that's what the lens is  now of course rage race is a massive  component that is causing understandable  rage among a lot of people but that  analysis doesn't tell you everything  that you need to know our economic  system at its core for example functions  to stymie and suppress real change in  activism and it goes way beyond race has  racial implications of course but you  miss that if you make this only about  race much of that economic system is  certainly rooted in supremacist along  racial lines but a race only analysis  falls short a lot of the hot cakes we're  seeing or are only about race another  perspective that is heavily represented  is that this is really about capitalism  right any capitalist system is  inevitably racist and inevitably leads  to this degree of social unrest arson  looting property damage police violence  against protesters protesters  against police protests our own protests  or violence protesters versus looters  that the the 